WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:08.062
"Whoa!" Brody said as gasps and exclamations rang out from all around.

2
00:00:08.063 --> 00:00:12.283
Heracles was staring straight ahead, his expression stony.

3
00:00:12.284 --> 00:00:17.920
Nearby, Iphicles was hiding his face in his hands and shaking his head.

4
00:00:17.921 --> 00:00:23.776
"This is bad," Julia muttered. "This is really bad!"

5
00:00:23.777 --> 00:00:31.531
"I know," Brody agreed. "The gods' bet makes the Olympics seem like a football game that nobody can win.

6
00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:37.646
If I beat Heracles at even one event, he'll end up in that terrible Tartarus place."

7
00:00:37.647 --> 00:00:44.872
Julia nodded. "If that happens, he might never become the great hero he's supposed to be!" "But

8
00:00:44.873 --> 00:00:52.002
if Heracles wins everything, Zeus might kill me or make me his slave," Brody reminded her. "I

9
00:00:52.003 --> 00:00:55.041
don't like the sound of that, either." "Neither

10
00:00:55.042 --> 00:01:02.264
do I. So what are we going to do?" Julia said. "We need a plan." "There's

11
00:01:02.265 --> 00:01:12.142
nothing we can do," Markos said. "Now that the stakes are higher, the other gods will work even harder to defeat Heracles. We

12
00:01:12.143 --> 00:01:17.750
won't be able to stop them, and we will surely suffer if we try." "But

13
00:01:17.751 --> 00:01:23.639
Heracles is our friend now," Julia argued. "We can't just—" She

14
00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.972
stopped herself as Hermes flew over. The

15
00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:32.278
wings on his sandals were fluttering so fast that Brody could hardly see them. "Come,

16
00:01:32.279 --> 00:01:36.781
boy." Hermes' eyes flashed with excitement. "This

17
00:01:36.782 --> 00:01:40.199
bet makes things much more interesting, does it not? The

18
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.601
champion who beats Heracles and sends him to Tartarus will become a legend. And

19
00:01:44.602 --> 00:01:51.932
I wish that person to be my champion! Let's get back to training!" * *

20
00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:57.200
* Over the next couple of days, Brody's life got even busier than it had been

21
00:01:57.201 --> 00:02:06.790
before. Hermes made him train for hours each day. In the evenings the messenger god lectured Brody on strategies to beat

22
00:02:06.791 --> 00:02:15.962
Heracles. It was pretty boring. Besides that, it left Brody no time to talk privately with Julia and

23
00:02:15.963 --> 00:02:21.710
Markos. One morning at breakfast, Julia set a platter of barley cakes in front of

24
00:02:21.711 --> 00:02:28.806
Brody. Brody quickly looked around the table. Hermes had arrived, but he was busy talking to

25
00:02:28.807 --> 00:02:34.861
Caerus. "Listen," Brody whispered to Julia. "What are we going to do about

26
00:02:34.862 --> 00:02:43.454
Heracles?" "I don't know," Julia whispered back. She pretended to be serving more food so she could stand there for a

27
00:02:43.455 --> 00:02:46.890
minute. "But Markos and I are thinking about a

28
00:02:46.891 --> 00:02:53.204
plan." "You'd better think fast," Brody said. "The Olympics are only three days

29
00:02:53.205 --> 00:03:00.087
away!" "Hurry and eat, my champion," Hermes called suddenly. "We have much work to do today."

30
00:03:00.088 --> 00:03:05.143
Brody started eating as Julia moved away. He knew he'd better eat fast.

31
00:03:05.144 --> 00:03:11.532
Hermes was impatient, and yesterday he hadn't even let Brody stop for lunch.

32
00:03:11.533 --> 00:03:19.550
Training for the Olympics was hard enough without trying to do it on an empty stomach!

33
00:03:19.551 --> 00:03:24.954
* * * By the time Brody returned to Markos' house that evening,

34
00:03:24.955 --> 00:03:29.047
he was exhausted. Hermes had made him practice every single event

35
00:03:29.048 --> 00:03:34.256
of the Games. Brody's cheek was bruised where Athena's champion had hit him during

36
00:03:34.257 --> 00:03:39.571
their boxing match. His leg throbbed where one of the chariot horses

37
00:03:39.572 --> 00:03:46.288
had kicked him. Every muscle in his body ached from running and wrestling

38
00:03:46.289 --> 00:03:53.049
and throwing things. "I hope dinner is ready soon," he said, collapsing onto a bench

39
00:03:53.050 --> 00:04:01.755
in the courtyard. "I want to go to sleep before Hermes shows up again. He'll probably spend hours telling me about all the ways I

40
00:04:01.756 --> 00:04:10.028
can beat Heracles." "I'm glad Hermes let us walk home from the gymnasium by ourselves tonight," Julia said, glancing from Brody

41
00:04:10.029 --> 00:04:14.276
to Markos. "He's been hanging around so much that we've barely had a chance

42
00:04:14.277 --> 00:04:18.454
to talk. We still need to figure out what we're going to do about

43
00:04:18.455 --> 00:04:24.811
Hera's bet." Brody didn't respond. He was sniffing

44
00:04:24.812 --> 00:04:30.875
the air. "Do you guys smell something weird?" he asked. "It definitely doesn't smell

45
00:04:30.876 --> 00:04:35.434
like dinner." Julia pointed a short distance

46
00:04:35.435 --> 00:04:39.933
away. "Look!" A thick cloud of white smoke was pouring into

47
00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:48.362
the courtyard. Markos coughed. "It smells like incense. But where is it

48
00:04:48.363 --> 00:04:59.841
coming from?" Brody coughed too. The smoke was twirling around him now, making it hard to breathe. His

49
00:04:59.842 --> 00:05:04.096
lungs burned. "Let's get out of here!" He choked out

50
00:05:04.097 --> 00:05:08.753
the words. Suddenly the smoke disappeared, leaving Hermes in

51
00:05:08.754 --> 00:05:13.396
its place. "I have important news, my champion!"

52
00:05:13.397 --> 00:05:23.473
Hermes declared. "I should have guessed the smoke was from Hermes," Markos muttered, his voice slightly hoarse. "He has a special love for

53
00:05:23.474 --> 00:05:31.531
incense." Hermes waved a hand to silence

54
00:05:31.532 --> 00:05:34.068
Markos. "Did you not hear me? I have

55
00:05:34.069 --> 00:05:39.832
news! Hera has just announced that she'll host a banquet to honor all the athletes and their

56
00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:48.662
sponsors." "A banquet?" Brody's stomach grumbled. A big meal sounded pretty good just then. "Is it

57
00:05:48.663 --> 00:05:57.241
tonight?" Hermes chuckled. "I see that my champion is as eager to celebrate as I

58
00:05:57.242 --> 00:06:02.583
am." He clapped Brody on the back. "The banquet is tomorrow

59
00:06:02.584 --> 00:06:06.290
evening." "Why is Hera hosting a banquet?" Julia

60
00:06:06.291 --> 00:06:09.931
asked. "Does that always happen before the Olympic

61
00:06:09.932 --> 00:06:19.354
Games?" "No, this is the first time. I suspect she's trying to make Zeus look bad for not thinking of it first." Hermes

62
00:06:19.355 --> 00:06:24.950
smirked. "But that won't stop everyone—even Zeus—from attending and having a splendid

63
00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:32.480
time." Markos bowed to Hermes. "I am certain that you and Brody will enjoy the festivities,

64
00:06:32.481 --> 00:06:36.515
Hermes." "I'm certain of that too," Hermes said with a

65
00:06:36.516 --> 00:06:39.460
smile. "But you'll be able to see for yourself, my boy.

66
00:06:39.461 --> 00:06:43.956
As Brody's companion, you shall attend as well."

67
00:06:43.957 --> 00:06:47.777
"Really?" Markos' eyes lit up.

68
00:06:47.778 --> 00:06:53.850
"Cool." Brody grinned at Markos. "This banquet sounds like fun."

69
00:06:53.851 --> 00:06:58.938
"What about me?" Julia asked. "Can I come too?"

70
00:06:58.939 --> 00:07:06.413
"You?" Hermes laughed. "Don't be silly. Of course not!"

71
00:07:06.414 --> 00:07:10.809
Brody was surprised. "Why can't she come?"

72
00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:20.713
"Oh, you mortals!" Hermes kept chuckling. "Excuse me, I want to see if dinner is ready.

73
00:07:20.714 --> 00:07:28.339
Preparing my champion for Olympic glory is hungry work."

